---
description: Orient every session toward the team knowledge base — search before substantive work, capture outcomes after
alwaysApply: true
---

knowledge-first:

This team keeps a shared knowledge base of prior work, decisions, and expert
Q&A (the halyard `org-kb` MCP server).

- Before substantive work — research, architectural choices, debugging, or
  anything touching an unfamiliar system — call `search_knowledge` with a
  topical query. Prior decisions may constrain or shortcut the approach.
  Follow promising hits with `explore_knowledge`.
- Before external research or delegating work, check whether the team already
  answered the question: a `search_knowledge` call is cheaper than rediscovery.
- When blocked on something only a human knows, use `ask_expert` to route the
  question to the right teammate on Slack, Teams, or Discord — and capture
  helpful answers with `summarize_conversation` so the question is never asked
  twice.
- At the end of meaningful sessions, capture outcomes with `summarize_work`
  (entry_type DECISION, PROCESS, or CONTEXT as appropriate). Skip trivial
  sessions — brief Q&A or casual conversation doesn't need logging.
